# Citation metadata for this repository, in Citation File Format 1.2.0.
# GitHub reads this file and renders a "Cite this repository" button; Zenodo,
# Zotero and the `cffr` R package read it directly.
#
# TO FINISH: two fields below are marked TODO because they cannot be guessed --
# your ORCID, and a DOI if you archive a release on Zenodo. Everything else is
# accurate as written. Validate after editing with:
#     R -e 'cffr::cff_validate("CITATION.cff")'
#   or
#     pip install cffconvert && cffconvert --validate

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the workforce estimates it produces, please cite it as below."
title: "midwifery: linking the AMCB certification roster to NPI identity and county geography"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline that turns the 22,309 names in the American Midwifery
  Certification Board's public verification directory -- which publishes no
  addresses at any level -- into geolocated, county-assigned midwife records.
  Identity is resolved against NPPES by ranked evidence classes rather than a
  blended similarity score, so every accepted link states the evidence that
  carried it and ambiguous candidates are quarantined rather than guessed.
  Practice addresses are then geocoded and assigned to counties, census tracts
  and congressional districts, and combined with AHRF, ACS, CMS Provider of
  Services and CDC WONDER natality data to produce county-level midwifery
  supply and access measures. Linkage certainty and geographic completeness are
  reported as separate properties: 65.7% of the roster links with confirmed
  midwifery taxonomy, and geography is essentially complete (~99%) for whatever
  links.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Muffly
    given-names: Tyler
    email: tyler.muffly@dhha.org
    affiliation: "Denver Health and Hospital Authority, Denver, Colorado, USA"
    # TODO: add your ORCID, e.g. orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1825-0097"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX"
  - family-names: Thumm
    given-names: Bree
    # TODO: affiliation and ORCID, supplied by the author rather than guessed.
    # affiliation: ""
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mufflyt/midwifery"
url: "https://github.com/mufflyt/midwifery"
version: "0.7.0"
date-released: "2026-08-14"
license: MIT
# TODO: if you deposit a release on Zenodo, add the DOI here and in README.md:
